cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "CoRTeC: A Differentially Private Release for Synthetic Tabular Data, Decodable With or Without a Language Model"
message: "If you use this software or the accompanying paper, please cite it."
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
version: "1.2.3"
date-released: "2026-10-28"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22945315"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Calyie/cortec"
abstract: >-
  CoRTeC spends a differential privacy budget once, on a small release of class-conditional
  histograms and a conditional outcome table inside publicly defined cohorts, and lets Private-PGM
  or a frozen language model decode that release, the model under exact per-bin counts and a
  selection step that returns the generated rows to the released cells. The model never sees a private record, so every draw is
  post-processing of the release. The paper measures what each part of the design contributes: the
  same release decoded by a maximum-entropy model with no language model, the schema with every
  name replaced by a neutral token, the reference implementations of AIM and MST, and three recent
  methods under their own protocols. The release carries the fidelity and the
  utility; the language model adds plausibility driven by the column names; the reference AIM is
  ahead on pairwise fidelity and, for the fixed-rule release at larger sample sizes, on utility, and
  level with or behind the auto-configured release decoded with no model; what survives every control
  is the privacy architecture. This repository holds the Apache-2.0 reference implementation with its
  tests, the research pipeline, the papers and the frozen auto-configurations.
authors:
